1
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:02,480
From now on, no matter what happens,

2
00:01:02,560 --> 00:01:05,200
I won't let you face it alone.

3
00:01:05,280 --> 00:01:07,360
You really chose her over me.

4
00:01:07,440 --> 00:01:08,600
I chose my own life.

5
00:01:08,680 --> 00:01:11,600
And I won't let anyone
hurt the one I love.

6
00:01:11,680 --> 00:01:13,720
I feel so lucky

7
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:15,960
to have you by my side.

8
00:01:19,680 --> 00:01:21,480
I understand.

9
00:01:21,560 --> 00:01:24,560
I just didn't want her
to have a difficult life,

10
00:01:25,520 --> 00:01:28,800
but in the end,
I'm the one who's at fault.

11
00:01:37,480 --> 00:01:41,120
You seem to be really happy
without me, huh, Runch?

12
00:01:44,920 --> 00:01:46,880
I did my best to raise you right.

13
00:01:46,960 --> 00:01:48,960
I've done everything for you.

14
00:01:49,040 --> 00:01:50,040
But in the end,

15
00:01:50,120 --> 00:01:52,880
I wasn't the one you chose to stand by.

16
00:01:54,040 --> 00:01:56,320
Great. Just great.

17
00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:04,960
<i>I took this picture</i>
<i>for you to see how she's doing.</i>

18
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:16,400
Runch, if your happiness

19
00:02:16,480 --> 00:02:19,200
comes at the cost of treating me horribly,

20
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:21,080
I won't back down.

21
00:02:21,160 --> 00:02:23,760
There's no way
I'm losing you to that girl.

22
00:02:27,960 --> 00:02:30,120
Our grand opening is just one day away.

23
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:31,760
There'll be lots of guests and press,

24
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:34,560
so there's no room for error.

25
00:02:34,640 --> 00:02:37,840
For tomorrow's tasting,
please tell the kitchen

26
00:02:37,920 --> 00:02:40,080
to try serving on our actual timeline.

27
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:41,840
It won't be just about the flavors.

28
00:02:41,920 --> 00:02:44,160
As for the PR,
I want the key message to be clear,

29
00:02:44,240 --> 00:02:47,600
because we don't just sell the food
but also the experience.

30
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:50,320
If you have any concerns
or think you can't make it in time,

31
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:52,320
please let me know now.

32
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:54,240
I don't want to solve problems on the day.

33
00:02:54,320 --> 00:02:57,000
I assure you everything
will be ready in time, Ms. Peeracha.

34
00:02:57,640 --> 00:02:59,280
Perfect.

35
00:02:59,360 --> 00:03:02,280
When can we finalize the VIP guest list?

36
00:03:02,360 --> 00:03:04,760
We should get it done by this evening.

37
00:03:04,840 --> 00:03:05,680
Perfect.

38
00:03:05,760 --> 00:03:07,000
I want every team

39
00:03:07,080 --> 00:03:08,880
to send me an update by 3:00 p.m. today,

40
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:11,000
then we'll have a final meeting
tomorrow morning.

41
00:03:11,600 --> 00:03:13,360
That's all. Thank you.

42
00:03:20,440 --> 00:03:22,320
Excuse me. Someone sent you flowers.

43
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:24,360
Who was it?

44
00:03:31,840 --> 00:03:33,680
Thanks for the flowers.

45
00:03:33,760 --> 00:03:35,040
My pleasure.

46
00:03:35,640 --> 00:03:36,920
I had them delivered to you.

47
00:03:39,440 --> 00:03:42,160
Now Nat will never stop teasing me.

48
00:03:45,160 --> 00:03:46,960
She'll keep teasing you,

49
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:48,440
no matter what I do.

50
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:50,920
Well, she likes you.

51
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:54,440
She even said she's jealous of me
for marrying you.

52
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:56,000
Yeah?

53
00:03:57,800 --> 00:03:59,280
Anyway,

54
00:03:59,360 --> 00:04:02,160
thanks again for the pretty flowers.

55
00:04:03,760 --> 00:04:06,360
These pretty flowers

56
00:04:06,440 --> 00:04:09,120
are perfect for a pretty girl like you.

57
00:04:11,720 --> 00:04:13,640
You look so pretty today, Neen.

58
00:04:14,440 --> 00:04:16,880
- You say that every day.
- Well,

59
00:04:16,959 --> 00:04:18,880
that's just the truth.

60
00:04:18,959 --> 00:04:20,880
You look pretty every day.

61
00:04:23,160 --> 00:04:24,720
You're sweet-talking me.

62
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:26,960
Do you want something?

63
00:04:32,280 --> 00:04:34,480
Can I tell you that tonight?

64
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:36,720
I guess I'll wait.

65
00:04:37,960 --> 00:04:39,320
Right now,

66
00:04:40,520 --> 00:04:42,000
I just want to kiss you.

67
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:45,640
I want to kiss you too.

68
00:04:47,280 --> 00:04:49,280
You can do even more than that.

69
00:04:57,280 --> 00:04:59,800
No. I have to get back to work.
Come on. Get up.

70
00:04:59,880 --> 00:05:00,840
I'm too tired.

71
00:05:00,920 --> 00:05:03,600
Come on. Get up.

72
00:05:06,680 --> 00:05:08,000
Come in.

73
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:18,440
Boss, can I speak to you for a moment?

74
00:05:19,480 --> 00:05:20,640
What is it?

75
00:05:23,280 --> 00:05:26,600
I wanted to apologize to you

76
00:05:26,680 --> 00:05:29,040
for everything I've done.

77
00:05:32,880 --> 00:05:35,400
I'm sorry for my behavior,
for insulting you,

78
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:38,000
and for crossing the line.

79
00:05:38,840 --> 00:05:40,520
I did some thinking and realized

80
00:05:41,600 --> 00:05:43,920
all the things I've done
were unfair to you.

81
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:48,640
Sure.

82
00:05:49,320 --> 00:05:50,920
Is there anything else?

83
00:05:53,400 --> 00:05:54,680
I just wanted

84
00:05:54,760 --> 00:05:57,440
to let you know
that I'm here if you need help

85
00:05:57,520 --> 00:05:58,720
with anything.

86
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:00,920
I'd be happy to help.

87
00:06:04,800 --> 00:06:05,760
Sure.

88
00:06:06,440 --> 00:06:09,280
If there's anything, I'll let you know.

89
00:06:11,880 --> 00:06:13,480
That's all I wanted to hear.

90
00:06:14,080 --> 00:06:15,080
Alright.

91
00:06:19,760 --> 00:06:23,280
Oh, Mrs. Ging. What a coincidence.

92
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:27,240
It seems all kinds of people
come to this coffee shop.

93
00:06:29,920 --> 00:06:33,160
I think it's nice. This way,
you'll see different world views.

94
00:06:33,240 --> 00:06:35,840
Some views aren't worth seeing, though.

95
00:06:35,920 --> 00:06:38,640
If you don't want to see it, then don't.

96
00:06:39,520 --> 00:06:42,640
The world has changed.
Even if you try to ignore it,

97
00:06:42,720 --> 00:06:45,040
the Earth won't stop spinning.

98
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:50,720
You're as eloquent as always.

99
00:06:51,960 --> 00:06:53,200
Not really.

100
00:06:53,280 --> 00:06:56,400
I just never say things
I will regret later.

101
00:06:57,440 --> 00:06:59,240
I hope this coffee

102
00:06:59,960 --> 00:07:03,200
makes your day a little better.

103
00:07:17,160 --> 00:07:19,200
You ran into Runch's mother?

104
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:21,080
Did she do something to you?

105
00:07:21,160 --> 00:07:22,760
What could she possibly do to me?

106
00:07:22,840 --> 00:07:24,680
I'm not that fragile.

107
00:07:26,440 --> 00:07:27,720
What about you, though?

108
00:07:27,800 --> 00:07:29,400
Did you do something to her?

109
00:07:29,480 --> 00:07:32,880
When she saw me,
she just kept glaring at me.

110
00:07:34,160 --> 00:07:36,520
She'll hate me no matter what I do.

111
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:39,520
I don't know why she doesn't love me.

112
00:07:39,600 --> 00:07:42,160
I'm a very lovable person.

113
00:07:42,240 --> 00:07:43,600
Oh, really?

114
00:07:43,680 --> 00:07:44,600
Mom.

115
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:50,440
Seeing Mrs. Ging act that way

116
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:52,360
makes me feel so bad for Runch.

117
00:07:53,880 --> 00:07:56,960
Yeah. I don't even want Runch
to have to choose.

118
00:07:57,040 --> 00:08:00,760
I just don't want to feel like
I'm competing with anyone.

119
00:08:01,360 --> 00:08:03,880
Hey, you're not competing with anyone.

120
00:08:03,960 --> 00:08:06,720
If being in a relationship
feels like a competition,

121
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:09,720
that means someone isn't letting go.

122
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:15,320
Well,

123
00:08:16,200 --> 00:08:18,880
aren't you mad at me
that things have come to this?

124
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:21,520
I'm more mad at the world

125
00:08:21,600 --> 00:08:24,440
for turning love
into something you have to prove.

126
00:08:26,320 --> 00:08:27,560
Don't worry, though.

127
00:08:28,160 --> 00:08:29,960
The fact that we're getting along

128
00:08:30,040 --> 00:08:33,440
means we're luckier than a lot of people.

129
00:08:35,679 --> 00:08:36,880
I love you, Mom.

130
00:08:40,440 --> 00:08:43,440
If you're this sweet, then I can't argue.

131
00:08:43,520 --> 00:08:44,440
See?

132
00:08:47,920 --> 00:08:49,040
Good girl.

133
00:08:55,240 --> 00:08:57,400
I ran into Kaekai today.

134
00:08:59,200 --> 00:09:00,720
She was so rude.

135
00:09:00,800 --> 00:09:02,640
That woman has a mouth on her.

136
00:09:02,720 --> 00:09:04,120
She had nothing to say

137
00:09:04,720 --> 00:09:06,600
but snarky comments.

138
00:09:07,680 --> 00:09:10,440
So that's where her daughter got it from.

139
00:09:10,520 --> 00:09:12,600
She got it from her.

140
00:09:12,680 --> 00:09:14,280
Those two

141
00:09:14,360 --> 00:09:16,440
always act so holier-than-thou.

142
00:09:16,520 --> 00:09:18,080
Well, did you say something

143
00:09:18,160 --> 00:09:20,440
- to make her--
- Pong.

144
00:09:21,280 --> 00:09:23,000
Are you saying it was my fault?

145
00:09:23,960 --> 00:09:26,480
That's not it. I'm just…

146
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:29,760
Pong, you're taking her side too?

147
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:32,000
Why is no one ever on my side?

148
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:34,440
- I'm not--
- Not my husband, not my daughter!

149
00:09:34,520 --> 00:09:37,200
I'm not taking anyone's side.
I just want you to calm down.

150
00:09:37,280 --> 00:09:40,880
Calm down?
Do you have any idea how I feel?

151
00:09:42,120 --> 00:09:43,520
I'm a mother.

152
00:09:44,280 --> 00:09:45,960
I've done everything for my daughter.

153
00:09:46,680 --> 00:09:47,840
But in the end,

154
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:50,200
nobody wants me.

155
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:53,240
No one said that. You're the one

156
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:54,640
who pushed everyone away.

157
00:09:54,720 --> 00:09:58,120
I didn't. I just don't want to give up.

158
00:09:58,720 --> 00:09:59,640
You don't have to win

159
00:09:59,720 --> 00:10:01,960
to be the mother she wants.

160
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:05,200
You don't get me either.

161
00:10:26,560 --> 00:10:28,760
What's that smell? Smells so good.

162
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:30,040
It's an aroma.

163
00:10:30,640 --> 00:10:32,160
It's lavender.

164
00:10:37,760 --> 00:10:40,000
You see, Nat told me

165
00:10:40,080 --> 00:10:42,440
you're opening a restaurant.

166
00:10:43,280 --> 00:10:46,800
This smell can help you de-stress,

167
00:10:47,400 --> 00:10:49,840
making you feel calm, relaxed,

168
00:10:49,920 --> 00:10:51,800
and at ease.

169
00:10:55,800 --> 00:10:59,120
Wow. It does make me feel better.

170
00:11:01,080 --> 00:11:03,040
But you know,

171
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:05,040
I don't need to look any further

172
00:11:05,120 --> 00:11:07,120
for the aroma that helps the most.

173
00:11:17,120 --> 00:11:18,840
It's your scent, of course.

174
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:23,840
It's so refreshing, honey.

175
00:11:26,160 --> 00:11:28,240
You're in such a good mood.

176
00:11:28,840 --> 00:11:31,360
Are you ready to hear my request?

177
00:11:33,760 --> 00:11:34,960
What is it?

178
00:11:35,800 --> 00:11:37,840
I'm willing to give you anything.

179
00:11:52,200 --> 00:11:53,880
This is what you wanted?

180
00:11:55,560 --> 00:11:57,880
I wanted to give you a massage

181
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:02,040
because I knew you'd be so tired

182
00:12:02,560 --> 00:12:05,560
after working at your office all day.

183
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:13,360
Right there.

184
00:12:14,360 --> 00:12:15,600
It's really sore.

185
00:12:17,240 --> 00:12:19,800
You know me too well, Runch.

186
00:12:37,080 --> 00:12:38,640
Anywhere else?

187
00:12:42,280 --> 00:12:43,440
My cheeks.

188
00:12:54,960 --> 00:12:57,680
I think using your lips

189
00:12:57,760 --> 00:12:59,520
would work even better.

190
00:13:27,400 --> 00:13:28,640
Anywhere else?

191
00:13:33,280 --> 00:13:34,360
My lips.

192
00:13:59,280 --> 00:14:00,800
Are all the tables ready?

193
00:14:00,880 --> 00:14:03,720
Everything will be ready in ten minutes.

194
00:14:03,800 --> 00:14:07,400
Then tell the kitchen to reheat the sauce,

195
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:08,880
but don't let it boil.

196
00:14:08,960 --> 00:14:09,800
Okay.

197
00:14:09,880 --> 00:14:12,360
When does the first set of guests arrive?

198
00:14:12,440 --> 00:14:13,800
In 45 minutes.

199
00:14:13,880 --> 00:14:15,920
Okay. We still have time.

200
00:14:20,360 --> 00:14:24,480
Everyone, please pace yourselves.

201
00:14:24,560 --> 00:14:26,840
No need to rush or panic.
Just stay focused

202
00:14:26,920 --> 00:14:28,880
and do your best.

203
00:14:30,200 --> 00:14:31,280
Yes, ma'am.

204
00:14:31,360 --> 00:14:34,040
I'll go handle everything you asked for.

205
00:14:34,120 --> 00:14:35,120
Go for it.

206
00:14:41,360 --> 00:14:42,840
Oh, Runch!

207
00:14:45,200 --> 00:14:46,800
When did you get here?

208
00:14:46,880 --> 00:14:48,560
A while ago.

209
00:14:48,640 --> 00:14:51,800
Well, why didn't you say anything, then?

210
00:14:51,880 --> 00:14:54,640
Well, you were busy working.

211
00:14:54,720 --> 00:14:58,080
I was going to ask if you needed a hand.

212
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:01,240
But apparently,

213
00:15:01,320 --> 00:15:02,920
you don't need it.

214
00:15:03,600 --> 00:15:06,600
Oh, actually, there's one thing.

215
00:15:07,200 --> 00:15:08,280
What is it?

216
00:15:11,200 --> 00:15:13,360
Can you stay and be my moral support?

217
00:15:14,280 --> 00:15:16,440
Stay here and don't go anywhere.

218
00:15:17,360 --> 00:15:18,560
Of course.

219
00:15:19,160 --> 00:15:21,640
I wasn't planning to anyway.

220
00:15:30,680 --> 00:15:32,960
YOU HAVE A NEW MESSAGE

221
00:15:33,040 --> 00:15:36,200
<i>Ma'am, Ms. Runch is taking</i>
<i>the afternoon off today</i>

222
00:15:36,280 --> 00:15:38,840
<i>She's attending the grand opening</i>
<i>of Ms. Peeracha's restaurant.</i>

223
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:42,600
<i>Do you know where that is, Mr. Utt?</i>

224
00:17:20,119 --> 00:17:23,079
Neen sure did a great job organizing this.

225
00:17:23,599 --> 00:17:26,520
The vibe here is laid-back,

226
00:17:26,599 --> 00:17:29,120
warm, relaxed,

227
00:17:29,200 --> 00:17:30,760
and not too formal.

228
00:17:30,840 --> 00:17:32,160
It's like a family party.

229
00:17:33,680 --> 00:17:35,640
I think so too.

230
00:17:35,720 --> 00:17:38,400
But seeing Runch and Neen together

231
00:17:38,480 --> 00:17:40,120
makes it look more like a wedding

232
00:17:40,200 --> 00:17:41,880
than a restaurant grand opening.

233
00:17:47,880 --> 00:17:49,000
I know, right?

234
00:17:52,040 --> 00:17:54,840
Excuse me.
A reporter wants to interview you

235
00:17:54,920 --> 00:17:56,480
as a family.

236
00:17:56,560 --> 00:17:57,560
Sure.

237
00:17:58,880 --> 00:18:00,560
Neen. Runch.

238
00:18:01,520 --> 00:18:03,280
- Come here.
- Come on.

239
00:18:34,200 --> 00:18:35,440
I'm so sorry,

240
00:18:35,520 --> 00:18:38,520
but this event requires
an online invitation.

241
00:18:38,600 --> 00:18:40,400
I can enter without one.

242
00:18:40,480 --> 00:18:42,200
Sorry, ma'am,

243
00:18:42,280 --> 00:18:44,280
I really can't let you in
without an invitation.

244
00:18:44,360 --> 00:18:46,200
I'm Peeracha's mother-in-law. Got it?

245
00:18:46,280 --> 00:18:50,680
Ma'am, please don't lie.
You? Peeracha's mother-in-law?

246
00:18:50,760 --> 00:18:52,440
You're just trying to get in for free.

247
00:18:52,520 --> 00:18:54,680
Idiot! I'm telling the truth.

248
00:18:54,760 --> 00:18:55,960
I'm not lying, so move!

249
00:18:56,040 --> 00:18:57,800
Excuse me! Ma'am?

250
00:18:57,880 --> 00:18:59,440
- So you're refusing to leave?
- Move!

251
00:18:59,520 --> 00:19:01,320
- Get out of my way! I said I'd--
- Please, ma'am.

252
00:19:01,400 --> 00:19:02,720
- Ma'am, please leave.
- Guard!

253
00:19:02,800 --> 00:19:04,680
- What?
- Sorry. We really can't let you in.

254
00:19:04,760 --> 00:19:06,200
- Move!
- No!

255
00:19:06,280 --> 00:19:07,760
- Please, ma'am.
- Ma'am, no!

256
00:19:07,840 --> 00:19:08,960
Please leave.

257
00:19:14,640 --> 00:19:17,000
Runch, come on.

258
00:19:19,880 --> 00:19:21,600
You go ahead without me.

259
00:19:21,680 --> 00:19:23,000
I can wait here.

260
00:19:23,600 --> 00:19:24,720
No way.

261
00:19:24,800 --> 00:19:27,040
You're my family, you know.

262
00:19:29,680 --> 00:19:31,720
Neen, bring her over here.

263
00:19:33,040 --> 00:19:34,840
Runch, come on.

264
00:19:34,920 --> 00:19:35,760
Come on.

265
00:19:50,600 --> 00:19:52,400
Today's event feels so warm

266
00:19:52,480 --> 00:19:54,800
as if it was a family party.

267
00:19:54,880 --> 00:19:57,560
It doesn't feel like
a restaurant's grand opening at all.

268
00:19:59,040 --> 00:19:59,960
Actually, yes.

269
00:20:00,040 --> 00:20:02,520
In a way, this is a family party.

270
00:20:04,120 --> 00:20:06,760
I hope you don't mind
my daughter-in-law being here too.

271
00:20:07,560 --> 00:20:10,880
She's like a daughter to us,

272
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:13,000
as if we were related by blood.

273
00:20:14,520 --> 00:20:16,280
So it is a grand opening, after all.

274
00:20:17,840 --> 00:20:20,160
Then, can I take some photos
of your family--

275
00:20:20,240 --> 00:20:22,720
Oops! I mean,
your restaurant's grand opening?

276
00:20:22,800 --> 00:20:24,560
Please look at the camera. This way.

277
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:26,200
This camera, please.

278
00:20:26,280 --> 00:20:28,240
- This way.
- One, two, three.

279
00:20:29,120 --> 00:20:31,240
A little closer, everyone.

280
00:20:31,320 --> 00:20:32,760
One, two, three.

281
00:20:47,280 --> 00:20:49,800
Where were you? Why are you back so late?

282
00:20:49,880 --> 00:20:51,560
You weren't answering my calls either.

283
00:20:51,640 --> 00:20:54,120
I was at the grand opening
of Peeracha's restaurant.

284
00:20:55,080 --> 00:20:56,520
Did you cause any trouble there?

285
00:20:58,400 --> 00:21:00,320
Why do you think so,

286
00:21:00,920 --> 00:21:03,080
when I'm the one who's the victim here?

287
00:21:03,680 --> 00:21:05,480
Guess what? Today,

288
00:21:06,080 --> 00:21:08,680
our daughter became
part of another family.

289
00:21:08,760 --> 00:21:10,800
She's not ours anymore.

290
00:21:11,480 --> 00:21:13,440
She was standing next to another family.

291
00:21:16,800 --> 00:21:19,840
Both Peeracha and her family

292
00:21:19,920 --> 00:21:21,640
took Runch away from me.

293
00:21:26,400 --> 00:21:28,120
They did it right in front of me,

294
00:21:28,200 --> 00:21:31,080
and no one even noticed me.

295
00:21:32,120 --> 00:21:35,080
Please just leave her alone
and learn to let it go.

296
00:21:35,160 --> 00:21:37,720
Like hell I will! She's my daughter!

297
00:21:37,800 --> 00:21:39,880
How could I just let it slide?

298
00:21:39,960 --> 00:21:42,920
I didn't raise her
just so she'd choose some girl

299
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:44,680
over her own mother.

300
00:21:44,760 --> 00:21:46,240
Who would be okay with that?!

301
00:21:47,720 --> 00:21:50,840
Runch is avoiding you,
yet you still don't get it!

302
00:21:50,920 --> 00:21:52,600
What else is there to get

303
00:21:52,680 --> 00:21:54,480
other than the fact that she's stupid?

304
00:21:55,240 --> 00:21:57,400
She doesn't know
her wife is manipulating her.

305
00:21:57,480 --> 00:21:58,480
She's so well educated,

306
00:21:58,560 --> 00:22:00,560
and we've spent so much money on her,

307
00:22:01,120 --> 00:22:02,840
yet she acts like a brainless person.

308
00:22:02,920 --> 00:22:05,880
Actually, trying to ruin
someone else's family

309
00:22:05,960 --> 00:22:08,000
is what a brainless person would do.

310
00:22:08,080 --> 00:22:11,160
- Pong!
- Stop acting like this!

311
00:22:11,240 --> 00:22:12,800
One day, you'll be left all alone.

312
00:22:16,120 --> 00:22:17,080
No.

313
00:22:17,640 --> 00:22:19,440
Runch is just being led astray.

314
00:22:19,520 --> 00:22:22,360
Soon, she'll realize
who really loves her the most.

315
00:22:23,920 --> 00:22:26,080
There's no way I'm letting that brat win.

316
00:22:26,840 --> 00:22:30,280
No matter what,
I need to get my daughter back.

317
00:22:32,320 --> 00:22:34,080
Do whatever you want.

318
00:22:34,160 --> 00:22:36,440
Fake being sick
or being dead, for all I care.

319
00:22:38,160 --> 00:22:40,120
But let me warn you.

320
00:22:40,200 --> 00:22:41,760
If you keep doing it,

321
00:22:41,840 --> 00:22:44,200
one day, when you're really sick or dead,

322
00:22:44,280 --> 00:22:45,880
no one will care for you.

323
00:22:46,640 --> 00:22:48,440
And I don't mean just our daughter.

324
00:22:49,080 --> 00:22:52,240
Even I, who you keep fooling,
won't care either.

325
00:22:53,640 --> 00:22:55,320
And you'd better not forget

326
00:22:56,560 --> 00:23:00,040
Neen's last name
or what family she's from.

327
00:23:00,720 --> 00:23:02,880
You'd better watch your step.

328
00:23:02,960 --> 00:23:04,760
And watch your mouth too.

329
00:23:04,840 --> 00:23:06,400
You only got away with everything

330
00:23:06,480 --> 00:23:08,560
because Runch has been protecting you.

331
00:23:11,160 --> 00:23:12,960
But she's done with you now,

332
00:23:13,040 --> 00:23:16,000
so that family doesn't have
to hold back anymore.

333
00:23:17,720 --> 00:23:21,160
If she's really
going to let her wife bully me,

334
00:23:21,240 --> 00:23:22,680
then so be it.

335
00:23:22,760 --> 00:23:24,360
How dare you say that

336
00:23:24,920 --> 00:23:27,240
when you're the one
who's been bullying her?

337
00:23:28,840 --> 00:23:30,880
You and Runch are equally stupid!

338
00:23:30,960 --> 00:23:32,760
Why do you care about that brat so much?

339
00:23:36,720 --> 00:23:38,280
Go ahead. You can all walk away!

340
00:23:38,360 --> 00:23:40,120
You don't have to care for me!

341
00:23:40,200 --> 00:23:41,640
I won't beg you to forgive me.

342
00:24:01,440 --> 00:24:03,480
Isn't my granddaughter just adorable?

343
00:24:03,560 --> 00:24:07,080
She is. She looks exactly like you.

344
00:24:07,160 --> 00:24:09,200
That's what they all say.

345
00:24:10,120 --> 00:24:13,240
You know, at our age,

346
00:24:13,320 --> 00:24:16,400
just hearing her call you "Grandma"

347
00:24:16,480 --> 00:24:19,360
really warms your heart.

348
00:24:19,440 --> 00:24:20,560
I guess you're right.

349
00:24:21,760 --> 00:24:23,480
What about Runch?

350
00:24:23,560 --> 00:24:25,080
When is she going to get married?

351
00:24:25,160 --> 00:24:26,440
She's not young anymore.

352
00:24:28,600 --> 00:24:30,360
She's not even dating anyone,

353
00:24:30,440 --> 00:24:32,160
let alone getting married.

354
00:24:34,720 --> 00:24:36,360
I'm so worried about her.

355
00:24:39,680 --> 00:24:40,560
Mom.

356
00:24:41,720 --> 00:24:43,200
What is it, honey?

357
00:24:44,760 --> 00:24:46,640
I've got something to tell you.

358
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:49,160
What is it?

359
00:24:57,760 --> 00:24:59,960
There's someone I'd like you to meet.

360
00:25:00,640 --> 00:25:01,840
Is it your date?

361
00:25:03,800 --> 00:25:05,320
Really?

362
00:25:06,240 --> 00:25:08,320
We haven't known each other for long,

363
00:25:08,400 --> 00:25:10,760
but I'm so in love with them, Mom.

364
00:25:13,320 --> 00:25:15,960
They're so cute and bubbly.

365
00:25:16,040 --> 00:25:19,560
I feel at home whenever I'm with them.

366
00:25:19,640 --> 00:25:21,680
Look, Runch. No matter who you love,

367
00:25:21,760 --> 00:25:24,320
I'll love them too.

368
00:25:24,400 --> 00:25:27,120
Bring your date over sometime.
I want to meet him.

369
00:25:27,960 --> 00:25:29,400
Sure, Mom.

370
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:32,040
Hello, Dad. Hello, Mom.

371
00:25:32,120 --> 00:25:33,640
- Hello.
- Hello.

372
00:25:40,480 --> 00:25:42,160
What are you looking for?

373
00:25:42,240 --> 00:25:44,080
Your date, of course.

374
00:25:44,160 --> 00:25:45,720
Why isn't he here yet?

375
00:25:47,400 --> 00:25:48,880
Here she is.

376
00:25:49,480 --> 00:25:50,560
Her name is Neen.

377
00:26:03,280 --> 00:26:04,280
Honey?

378
00:26:06,040 --> 00:26:07,800
This is so unexpected.

379
00:26:08,320 --> 00:26:12,200
I can't believe
our daughter is into girls.

380
00:26:12,800 --> 00:26:15,400
That's a normal thing these days.

381
00:26:15,480 --> 00:26:18,000
As long as she's a good person
who truly loves our daughter,

382
00:26:18,080 --> 00:26:19,320
isn't that all that matters?

383
00:26:19,400 --> 00:26:20,400
No.

384
00:26:21,200 --> 00:26:22,720
I won't allow it.

385
00:26:24,160 --> 00:26:27,600
I don't believe
this kind of love can last.

386
00:26:27,680 --> 00:26:29,640
It's just a phase.

387
00:26:29,720 --> 00:26:31,600
Runch is probably just curious.

388
00:26:31,680 --> 00:26:33,760
Once she gets bored, they'll break up.

389
00:26:36,600 --> 00:26:39,320
You're belittling her feelings.

390
00:26:39,400 --> 00:26:40,680
I'm not.

391
00:26:40,760 --> 00:26:43,560
It's just that I know her well.

392
00:26:43,640 --> 00:26:45,800
She's never acted this way before.

393
00:26:45,880 --> 00:26:48,000
This is not her true self.

394
00:26:48,080 --> 00:26:51,520
Maybe you just can't
accept her for being herself.

395
00:26:54,280 --> 00:26:56,400
Either way, I really don't believe

396
00:26:56,480 --> 00:26:58,720
that they'll last.

397
00:26:58,800 --> 00:27:02,120
We're planning to get married.

398
00:27:03,520 --> 00:27:06,360
I'm really happy for you both.

399
00:27:06,440 --> 00:27:09,360
Keep your love strong
and always take care of each other, okay?

400
00:27:10,200 --> 00:27:12,760
- Thank you.
- Thank you, Dad.

401
00:27:12,840 --> 00:27:14,120
Have you thought this through?

402
00:27:15,160 --> 00:27:16,000
Yes.

403
00:27:16,560 --> 00:27:18,360
We both have.

404
00:27:18,880 --> 00:27:19,880
That's right.

405
00:27:19,960 --> 00:27:22,560
In fact, we've already
registered our marriage.

406
00:27:23,160 --> 00:27:24,160
What?

407
00:27:32,880 --> 00:27:33,840
Okay.

408
00:27:35,040 --> 00:27:36,800
When's the wedding going to be?

409
00:27:37,920 --> 00:27:40,280
We'll plan the wedding
as soon as our house is done.

410
00:27:40,360 --> 00:27:42,680
House? What house?

411
00:27:43,640 --> 00:27:44,920
My parents

412
00:27:45,000 --> 00:27:47,560
bought us a house to move into
after getting married.

413
00:27:47,640 --> 00:27:50,240
Does that mean you'll move out

414
00:27:50,320 --> 00:27:53,400
once you get married, Runch?

415
00:27:54,440 --> 00:27:55,600
Yes, Mom.

416
00:27:58,800 --> 00:28:00,000
You'll be fine.

417
00:28:05,320 --> 00:28:07,120
I know it's not easy,

418
00:28:07,200 --> 00:28:10,280
but our daughter's all grown up now.
We have to let her live.

419
00:28:10,880 --> 00:28:13,200
I can accept that she's into girls.

420
00:28:13,280 --> 00:28:15,160
That's a normal thing these days.

421
00:28:15,960 --> 00:28:18,280
I'm not that conservative.

422
00:28:18,880 --> 00:28:21,160
I just don't want it to be that girl.

423
00:28:23,880 --> 00:28:26,120
That girl's coming into my daughter's life

424
00:28:26,800 --> 00:28:28,960
and taking her away from me.

425
00:28:29,040 --> 00:28:32,040
She didn't take Runch.
Runch was the one who chose her.

426
00:28:32,880 --> 00:28:34,400
Without Peeracha,

427
00:28:34,480 --> 00:28:36,720
my daughter wouldn't have
considered marriage,

428
00:28:36,800 --> 00:28:40,040
moving out, or walking out of my life.

429
00:28:41,120 --> 00:28:43,360
I can accept anything,

430
00:28:43,440 --> 00:28:46,000
except for the fact

431
00:28:47,480 --> 00:28:48,920
that that woman

432
00:28:49,840 --> 00:28:54,200
is taking my place in Runch's life.

433
00:28:54,280 --> 00:28:56,880
Neen isn't taking anyone's place, Ging.

434
00:28:57,400 --> 00:28:59,200
But my daughter chose her,

435
00:29:00,200 --> 00:29:01,560
not me.

436
00:29:08,560 --> 00:29:10,400
From this moment on,

437
00:29:11,160 --> 00:29:12,240
there's no way

438
00:29:12,960 --> 00:29:15,360
I'll ever see that woman in a good light.

439
00:30:03,000 --> 00:30:04,600
So many positive comments!

440
00:30:05,160 --> 00:30:08,360
"Every dish was great."
"Warm service, felt like home."

441
00:30:08,440 --> 00:30:10,400
"The vibe there was so laid-back." Whoa!

442
00:30:11,880 --> 00:30:14,840
Well, they like it
because you put your heart into it.

443
00:30:14,920 --> 00:30:17,360
Look, look! Read this one.

444
00:30:17,440 --> 00:30:19,800
"Ms. Peeracha's family
seems so sweet and warm."

445
00:30:19,880 --> 00:30:21,400
"They seem so warm."

446
00:30:21,480 --> 00:30:23,760
"Her parents seem very kind."

447
00:30:25,360 --> 00:30:26,600
And this too.

448
00:30:34,240 --> 00:30:36,280
"Ms. Peeracha's wife is stunning.

449
00:30:36,360 --> 00:30:39,320
She looks elegant,
luxurious, yet so kind."

450
00:30:41,240 --> 00:30:42,240
Wait a second.

451
00:30:43,200 --> 00:30:44,440
They're only complimenting you.

452
00:30:44,520 --> 00:30:46,760
What about me, the restaurant owner?

453
00:30:48,640 --> 00:30:51,080
It's because you're obviously pretty.

454
00:30:51,160 --> 00:30:52,480
There's no need for compliments.

455
00:30:52,560 --> 00:30:55,080
Of course there is. That's not fair.

456
00:30:55,160 --> 00:30:56,960
Now I'm starting to worry.

457
00:30:57,760 --> 00:30:59,920
About what?

458
00:31:00,440 --> 00:31:03,480
Well, the whole world
is falling in love with my wife.

459
00:31:03,560 --> 00:31:05,120
I've got to do something about that.

460
00:31:05,200 --> 00:31:07,240
What are you going to do?

461
00:31:07,760 --> 00:31:10,960
I'm going to show the whole world

462
00:31:11,040 --> 00:31:14,320
that you're mine,
and that I love you very much.

463
00:31:17,640 --> 00:31:20,280
What if they already know?

464
00:31:21,440 --> 00:31:24,280
I'll still do it
just so everything's clear.

465
00:31:28,720 --> 00:31:31,080
- Stop. Stop it, Neen.
- No.

466
00:31:33,800 --> 00:31:35,640
You sure you won't stop?

467
00:31:36,240 --> 00:31:38,080
Yes, I am, gorgeous.

468
00:31:41,920 --> 00:31:42,960
What are you doing?

469
00:31:44,760 --> 00:31:45,840
What are you doing?

470
00:31:47,480 --> 00:31:50,080
You've really got me going now.

471
00:32:47,720 --> 00:32:48,720
Hello?

472
00:32:49,360 --> 00:32:50,760
<i>Hello, ma'am.</i>

473
00:32:51,840 --> 00:32:54,880
I just read about the grand opening
of Ms. Peeracha's restaurant.

474
00:32:55,960 --> 00:32:57,520
I found it very strange.

475
00:32:58,160 --> 00:33:00,040
You weren't in any of the photos.

476
00:33:04,240 --> 00:33:07,440
<i>There was only Ms. Runch</i>
<i>and Ms. Peeracha's family.</i>

477
00:33:09,400 --> 00:33:12,280
That's so disrespectful to you.

478
00:33:12,360 --> 00:33:14,560
No matter what,
you're still Ms. Runch's mother.

479
00:33:15,680 --> 00:33:17,800
It's almost like

480
00:33:17,880 --> 00:33:20,440
she's trying to cut you out.

481
00:33:22,440 --> 00:33:24,400
Yesterday, I went to the restaurant.

482
00:33:24,480 --> 00:33:26,200
They wouldn't let me in.

483
00:33:26,280 --> 00:33:27,760
They told me to leave.

484
00:33:29,120 --> 00:33:30,400
Whoa.

485
00:33:31,000 --> 00:33:33,080
They'd really go that far?

486
00:33:33,960 --> 00:33:35,720
If I were you, I wouldn't let it slide.

487
00:33:36,600 --> 00:33:38,560
<i>They humiliated you,</i>

488
00:33:39,360 --> 00:33:41,640
<i>so you've got to do the same.</i>

489
00:33:43,080 --> 00:33:44,560
That type of person

490
00:33:44,640 --> 00:33:46,240
needs to be taught a lesson

491
00:33:46,320 --> 00:33:47,920
<i>before they start to feel something.</i>

492
00:33:51,760 --> 00:33:53,840
I don't want you to be hurt.

493
00:33:54,600 --> 00:33:57,080
I just hate seeing a good person like you

494
00:33:57,160 --> 00:33:59,000
getting kicked when you're down.

495
00:33:59,920 --> 00:34:02,120
If you do nothing,

496
00:34:02,200 --> 00:34:04,760
people may think you've given up.

497
00:34:09,719 --> 00:34:11,600
No matter what you decide to do,

498
00:34:12,199 --> 00:34:13,679
I will support you.

499
00:34:27,239 --> 00:34:29,639
Hi. I'd like to book a table
at your restaurant.

500
00:34:31,400 --> 00:34:35,239
For two, please.
Around five in the evening.

501
00:34:36,520 --> 00:34:37,679
Yes.

502
00:34:37,760 --> 00:34:40,040
Under the name Runch, please.

503
00:34:40,800 --> 00:34:42,080
Thank you.

504
00:35:09,320 --> 00:35:12,000
<i>Now's your chance to get revenge.</i>

505
00:35:12,080 --> 00:35:15,600
<i>Ms. Runch is meeting with</i>
<i>Ms. Peeracha this evening at five.</i>

506
00:35:16,200 --> 00:35:19,840
<i>As for the location, I'll tell you later.</i>

507
00:35:35,720 --> 00:35:39,560
Boss, I didn't drive here today.

508
00:35:39,640 --> 00:35:41,840
Would you mind giving me a ride?

509
00:35:43,480 --> 00:35:45,640
I have to go to Sukhumvit today.

510
00:35:45,720 --> 00:35:46,720
I won't be driving home.

511
00:35:47,320 --> 00:35:49,160
Oh, perfect, then.

512
00:35:49,240 --> 00:35:50,720
That's where I need to be.

513
00:35:50,800 --> 00:35:52,840
Would you mind giving me a ride?

514
00:35:57,040 --> 00:35:57,880
Fine.

515
00:36:08,680 --> 00:36:11,360
What a strange day, huh?

516
00:36:14,800 --> 00:36:16,360
It feels like…

517
00:36:18,400 --> 00:36:19,960
there's no need to rush

518
00:36:20,760 --> 00:36:22,200
or beware of anything.

519
00:36:23,560 --> 00:36:24,840
I feel it too.

520
00:36:26,400 --> 00:36:27,640
It's like

521
00:36:28,800 --> 00:36:31,880
we get to pace ourselves again.

522
00:36:38,120 --> 00:36:40,360
If I told you

523
00:36:40,440 --> 00:36:43,040
this was the best meal I've had in months,

524
00:36:43,120 --> 00:36:44,320
would you believe me?

525
00:36:46,360 --> 00:36:49,720
If you told me it's because of the food…

526
00:36:51,800 --> 00:36:53,000
I wouldn't believe you.

527
00:36:56,200 --> 00:36:58,480
But if you told me
it's because of the vibe,

528
00:36:58,560 --> 00:36:59,520
then I would.

529
00:37:01,040 --> 00:37:02,440
Cheers, then.

530
00:37:05,040 --> 00:37:07,920
To our family. To us.

531
00:37:08,880 --> 00:37:10,040
Cheers.

532
00:37:20,600 --> 00:37:22,280
You know, I'm glad

533
00:37:23,840 --> 00:37:26,120
to see you genuinely happy.

534
00:37:30,560 --> 00:37:32,720
It's not the food that makes me happy.

535
00:37:33,760 --> 00:37:36,320
It's having you by my side.

536
00:37:38,040 --> 00:37:39,480
I used to think

537
00:37:40,120 --> 00:37:42,600
happiness always came at a price.

538
00:37:45,960 --> 00:37:48,160
But now, I'm starting to believe

539
00:37:49,840 --> 00:37:51,760
that as long as we choose each other,

540
00:37:52,600 --> 00:37:53,920
that's all that matters.

541
00:37:55,080 --> 00:37:56,600
Where are you, ma'am?

542
00:37:57,640 --> 00:37:59,760
Oh, you're almost here?

543
00:38:06,000 --> 00:38:10,720
Excuse me, do you own a car
with the license plate YL7227?

544
00:38:10,800 --> 00:38:12,960
- Yes.
- Could you check your car?

545
00:38:13,040 --> 00:38:15,400
Someone said it was just hit.

546
00:38:15,480 --> 00:38:17,320
- Really?
- Yes, ma'am.

547
00:38:21,720 --> 00:38:22,560
I'll come with you.

548
00:38:22,640 --> 00:38:24,920
That's fine. I can go on my own.

549
00:38:25,000 --> 00:38:26,960
- Are you sure? Okay.
- Yeah.

550
00:38:47,720 --> 00:38:49,400
I don't see any scratches.

551
00:38:54,280 --> 00:38:56,040
Mom? How'd you get here?

552
00:38:59,400 --> 00:39:00,440
Are you crazy?!

553
00:39:00,520 --> 00:39:01,840
You're the crazy one here!

554
00:39:02,440 --> 00:39:04,840
It's because of you that Runch hates me

555
00:39:04,920 --> 00:39:06,200
and wants to ignore me!

556
00:39:06,280 --> 00:39:07,640
It's because of you!

557
00:39:07,720 --> 00:39:09,640
She hates you? How is that my fault?

558
00:39:11,160 --> 00:39:12,080
Crazy bitch!

559
00:39:14,000 --> 00:39:14,880
Did you just push me?

560
00:39:15,600 --> 00:39:17,240
- You bitch, how dare you!
- Stop it!

561
00:39:17,320 --> 00:39:19,080
You had no right to do this to me!

562
00:39:19,160 --> 00:39:20,160
Like hell I'll stop!

563
00:39:22,640 --> 00:39:25,640
This is nothing
compared to you taking my daughter!

564
00:39:29,560 --> 00:39:31,120
You think you've won?

565
00:39:31,200 --> 00:39:33,800
You think you finally
took Runch from me, huh?

566
00:39:34,680 --> 00:39:36,840
What are you talking about? She chose me!

567
00:39:36,920 --> 00:39:38,160
You're the one who can't let go!

568
00:39:38,240 --> 00:39:40,480
Shut up already. Without you,

569
00:39:40,560 --> 00:39:42,880
my daughter never
would've turned against me!

570
00:39:47,400 --> 00:39:49,560
You shameless bitch.
You always act all nice

571
00:39:49,640 --> 00:39:52,680
and sweet, but you're just a selfish girl

572
00:39:52,760 --> 00:39:54,520
who wants to steal everything from others!

573
00:39:55,880 --> 00:39:58,440
If that's how you feel,
then that's your problem,

574
00:39:58,520 --> 00:40:00,280
not mine. You crazy bitch!

575
00:40:03,440 --> 00:40:05,720
How dare you lecture me?

576
00:40:05,800 --> 00:40:08,000
I've done everything to raise my daughter!

577
00:40:12,000 --> 00:40:12,960
Crazy bitch!

578
00:40:15,120 --> 00:40:15,960
Stop it, Mom!

579
00:40:16,960 --> 00:40:19,120
Mom!

580
00:40:19,200 --> 00:40:20,800
That's enough, Mom! Stop!

581
00:40:21,800 --> 00:40:23,000
What the hell are you doing?!

582
00:40:30,320 --> 00:40:31,240
Neen.

583
00:40:42,120 --> 00:40:43,960
Runch, Runch!

584
00:40:44,640 --> 00:40:46,800
Didn't you see what she did to me?

585
00:40:46,880 --> 00:40:48,120
What about you?

586
00:40:48,200 --> 00:40:49,320
What the hell was that?

587
00:40:49,400 --> 00:40:50,720
I did this for you!

588
00:40:50,800 --> 00:40:53,160
- No, you didn't! You never do!
- She attacked me, I swear!

589
00:40:53,240 --> 00:40:55,040
You never did any of this for me.

590
00:40:56,080 --> 00:40:57,240
You did it for yourself.

591
00:40:57,320 --> 00:40:59,720
For your own satisfaction

592
00:41:00,360 --> 00:41:02,480
and your own self-importance.

593
00:41:04,800 --> 00:41:05,840
This woman…

594
00:41:07,400 --> 00:41:09,200
is the one I love.

595
00:41:09,840 --> 00:41:13,600
She's my wife. So why do you treat her

596
00:41:13,680 --> 00:41:15,680
like our enemy?

597
00:41:16,280 --> 00:41:18,320
She took my daughter from me.

598
00:41:21,600 --> 00:41:23,640
No one took me from you.

599
00:41:30,880 --> 00:41:32,600
I left you.

600
00:41:37,720 --> 00:41:38,680
Runch,

601
00:41:39,400 --> 00:41:40,800
I didn't mean to.

602
00:41:48,680 --> 00:41:50,760
Stop saying those things.

603
00:41:53,920 --> 00:41:55,720
I'm a grown-up now.

604
00:41:55,800 --> 00:41:57,680
I have my own life,

605
00:41:58,320 --> 00:42:00,360
but you never accepted that.

606
00:42:05,200 --> 00:42:07,320
I did my best to raise you right.

607
00:42:07,400 --> 00:42:09,560
I've sacrificed everything for you!

608
00:42:09,640 --> 00:42:11,480
Yeah, that's right!

609
00:42:11,560 --> 00:42:13,360
That's exactly right!

610
00:42:13,440 --> 00:42:15,600
You've sacrificed everything for me.

611
00:42:16,200 --> 00:42:18,480
And you've been using that fact

612
00:42:18,560 --> 00:42:21,160
to control me all my life.

613
00:42:37,680 --> 00:42:39,320
I'm supposed to listen to you,

614
00:42:40,280 --> 00:42:41,880
stay close to you,

615
00:42:43,640 --> 00:42:45,360
and never love anyone more than you.

616
00:42:48,920 --> 00:42:50,160
If I don't,

617
00:42:50,240 --> 00:42:52,800
then suddenly I'm an ungrateful child.

618
00:42:52,880 --> 00:42:54,840
No…

619
00:42:58,880 --> 00:43:00,120
You know,

620
00:43:01,640 --> 00:43:03,600
what you did today

621
00:43:04,400 --> 00:43:06,280
just messed up my life.

622
00:43:16,600 --> 00:43:17,960
Take your mom home.

623
00:43:20,720 --> 00:43:21,840
Neen.

624
00:43:23,720 --> 00:43:26,520
Take her, or I'll slap that old hag back.

625
00:43:27,360 --> 00:43:30,760
Neen, don't solve problems with violence.

626
00:43:31,560 --> 00:43:33,360
You're upset right now.

627
00:43:33,440 --> 00:43:35,560
But once you've calmed down,

628
00:43:35,640 --> 00:43:37,320
you'll regret what you did.

629
00:43:37,400 --> 00:43:39,040
I won't regret it!

630
00:43:40,400 --> 00:43:42,000
That old hag needs to learn

631
00:43:42,080 --> 00:43:43,600
that she can't just slap anyone.

632
00:43:43,680 --> 00:43:45,240
Come on, then, you little brat!

633
00:43:45,320 --> 00:43:46,640
- That's enough, Mom!
- Come on.

634
00:43:46,720 --> 00:43:47,680
Come on.

635
00:43:47,760 --> 00:43:49,040
Don't!

636
00:43:49,120 --> 00:43:50,240
Try me!

637
00:43:50,880 --> 00:43:53,240
Mom, enough.

638
00:43:56,080 --> 00:43:57,840
I'm taking her home.

639
00:43:57,920 --> 00:43:59,120
I'll meet you later.

640
00:43:59,840 --> 00:44:01,800
Let's go.

641
00:44:41,840 --> 00:44:44,840
LAST YEAR

642
00:44:44,920 --> 00:44:46,400
I'm so happy

643
00:44:46,480 --> 00:44:49,280
our marriage is finally registered.

644
00:44:49,360 --> 00:44:51,280
So am I.

645
00:44:53,760 --> 00:44:54,960
Runch.

646
00:44:55,040 --> 00:44:56,200
MARRIAGE CERTIFICATE

647
00:44:56,280 --> 00:44:59,720
You think your mom
will be okay with us getting married?

648
00:45:00,480 --> 00:45:02,320
Of course.

649
00:45:02,400 --> 00:45:08,240
And I'm sure my mom
will love you just like I do.

650
00:45:09,760 --> 00:45:10,600
Okay.

651
00:45:12,240 --> 00:45:14,160
I have a question to ask.

652
00:45:14,240 --> 00:45:15,360
Go for it.

653
00:45:16,960 --> 00:45:19,520
You said you wanted
to get married when you're 35,

654
00:45:19,600 --> 00:45:21,600
but you're not 35 yet.

655
00:45:23,400 --> 00:45:25,040
The earlier I get married,

656
00:45:25,120 --> 00:45:28,280
the longer I'll have you as my wife.

657
00:45:29,440 --> 00:45:32,480
We'll be together as wives,

658
00:45:33,080 --> 00:45:35,880
and we'll grow old together.

659
00:45:37,640 --> 00:45:40,880
Okay. Let's grow old together.

660
00:45:53,080 --> 00:45:56,200
If I don't fight,
I'll be left with nothing.

661
00:45:56,280 --> 00:45:59,600
From now on, I won't take responsibility
for your actions anymore.

662
00:45:59,680 --> 00:46:00,640
Why wouldn't you sue?

663
00:46:00,720 --> 00:46:03,000
I don't want to make her choose between

664
00:46:03,080 --> 00:46:04,920
justice and being a good daughter.

665
00:46:05,000 --> 00:46:07,360
- You're fired, Utt.
- You'll regret this.

666
00:46:07,440 --> 00:46:10,760
I don't want my love
to keep hurting you anymore.

667
00:46:11,360 --> 00:46:13,720
I'll give your mother what she wants.

668
00:46:14,320 --> 00:46:16,440
You can go back to being her daughter now.

669
00:46:17,040 --> 00:46:19,600
<i>Let me do this one last thing for you.</i>

670
00:47:02,600 --> 00:47:04,600
Subtitle translation by:
Ramil Natnitiwitaya
